WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.870
When Lucasfilm finally announced that the
title of Star Wars: Episode IX: The Rise of

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:10.110
Skywalker, fans wasted no time speculating
intensely about what it could mean.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.171
Questions of who is rising, which Skywalker
the title refers to, and whether one of the

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:18.410
trilogy's main characters would be confirmed
as a member of the Skywalker family swirled

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.210
through the Star Wars fandom.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.280
Fans won't get the answers to their inquiries
or have their theories validated until December

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.490
20th, but Star Wars legend Mark Hamill has
already thrown in his two cents.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:33.000
Hamill, whose character Luke Skywalker seemingly
died at the end of The Last Jedi, took to

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.370
Twitter to respond to all the conjecture.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.110
The actor absolutely loves that fans are going
wild with their Rise of Skywalker theses,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.010
and even offered up his own ideas about who
the titular Skywalker might be.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.010
He tweeted:

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.850
"It's time for the 8 months of speculation
to begin.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.530
Is that Skywalker KYLO?

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.530
LEIA?

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.530
ANAKIN?

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.530
LUKE?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.309
A previously unknown SKYWALKER?

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:56.719
Is REY a Skywalker?

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:57.719
#CoolTitle."

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:02.040
As soon as Hamill pressed "send" on that tweet,
he effectively opened up another floodgate

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.670
for fan theories to pour through.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.280
Thousands of people responded to Hamill's
post, sharing predictions about how the film's

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.950
events tie into the title.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.850
One fan theorized that the final battle of
The Rise of Skywalker will be between Rey

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:18.229
and Kylo Ren, with some familiar force ghosts
jumping into the fray.

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:23.319
Maybe Darth Vader, Anakin Skywalker, will
appear and aid Rey, thus becoming the Skywalker

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:25.740
who rises, according theory.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.799
Another fan responded to that idea with a
minor revision: In a moment reminiscent of

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:34.740
Return of the Jedi, the ghost of Emperor Palpatine,
who is seemingly heard cackling at the end

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.639
of the Rise of Skywalker trailer, pops up
behind Kylo, while the ghost of Luke Skywalker

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.240
appears behind Rey during the duo's battle.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.760
(laughing)

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.409
One theorist suggested that The Rise of Skywalker
isn't about Anakin Skywalker, but about Kylo

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:55.200
Ren, a.k.a. Ben Solo, who has Skywalker blood
thanks to his mother, Leia.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.749
Their response to Hamill's tweet was,

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.560
"It's about Ben's redemption!

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.099
Ben is the last Skywalker!

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:02.880
He will rise from the dark and ask Rey out!"

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.740
Kylo Ren could drop his dark side moniker,
return to the light, and reassume his given

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.700
name of Ben Solo in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.250
That isn't too wild an idea considering he's
the only other known Skywalker apart from

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.940
the apparently fallen Luke and his mother
Leia.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.950
He wasn't always the First Order-leading baddie
who wanted to follow in his grandfather Darth

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.950
Vader's footsteps.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.690
"A call to the light."

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:28.970
One other popular theory about who the nominal
Skywalker is that it isn't a single person

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.000
at all.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.590
Some fans believe that "Skywalker" will be
a new name for the Jedi, and that Rey will

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.780
lead them to bring peace to the galaxy.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.110
Twitter user Dan Sandler suggested that the
Skywalker name might be included in the ancient

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:45.101
Jedi texts Rey took from the mystical Force
tree just before Yoda burned it down in The

00:02:45.101 --> 00:02:46.120
Last Jedi.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.220
The books contain all that Rey would need
to teach a new generation of Jedi.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.120
But as Sandler speculates, there may not be
Jedi anymore.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.980
The Skywalkers could be a combination of Jedi
and Sith.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.071
This idea connects pretty seamlessly to the
title of the most recent Star Wars film: The

00:03:01.071 --> 00:03:02.280
Last Jedi.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.370
Many assumed that the title referred to Luke
Skywalker, and perhaps Luke really is the

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.020
last person in the galaxy who will be known
as a Jedi, with future Force-sensitive individuals

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.650
called Skywalkers.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.070
For every Star Wars fan, there's a different
theory about The Rise of Skywalker.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.320
It would be too great an undertaking to try
to pick apart every idea, but director J.J.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.200
Abrams himself has revealed this about the
film:

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.520
"This movie is about the new generation.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.920
What they've inherited, the light and the
dark, and ask the question about facing the

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.200
greatest evil: are they ready?"

